// Title: AWL Bypass with Winrm.vbs and Malicious WsmPty.xsl/WsmTxt.xsl - File
// Sigma ID: d353dac0-1b41-46c2-820c-d7d2561fc6ed
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Julia Fomina, oscd.community
// Date: 2020-10-06 | Modified: 2022-11-28
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1216
// Description: Detects execution of attacker-controlled WsmPty.xsl or WsmTxt.xsl via winrm.vbs and copied
//   cscript.exe (can be renamed)
// False positives:
//   - Unlikely
// References:
//   - https://posts.specterops.io/application-whitelisting-bypass-and-arbitrary-unsigned-code-execution-technique-in-winrm-vbs-c8c24fb40404
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/file/file_event/file_event_win_winrm_awl_bypass.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceFileEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "WsmPty.xsl" or FolderPath endswith "WsmTxt.xsl") and (not((FolderPath startswith "C:\\Windows\\System32\\" or FolderPath startswith "C:\\Windows\\SysWOW64\\")))
